---
import MissionLayout from '../../layouts/MissionLayout.astro';

const updatedScreenshots = Object.keys(import.meta.glob('/public/assets/projects/Verity_MRV/*.png'))
  .sort()
  .map((path) => path.replace('/public', '').split('/').map(encodeURIComponent).join('/'));
---

<MissionLayout
  slug="verity-nature-mrv"
  heading="Verity Nature - Digital MRV"
  timeline="24 Months"
  status="Shipped &amp; Validated"
  heroImage="/assets/projects/verity-mrv-01.jpg"
  explorerGradient="linear-gradient(160deg, #0c1a06 0%, #1a2d10 100%)"
>
  <section class="case-section">
    <h2 class="case-section-title">1. The TL;DR <span class="case-section-sub">(Executive Summary)</span></h2>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">The Purpose</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">To replace slow, paper-driven global carbon-auditing methods with a unified, high-integrity digital ecosystem capable of orchestrating remote workflows, tracking active assets, and validating technical data streams in real time.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">The Problem</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">The market faced a deep operational hurdle: field data collection was highly fragmented, entirely offline, and decoupled from global institutional servers. There was no automated infrastructure to validate edge data or securely push features without risking cross-network synchronization errors.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">The Solution</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">We engineered and launched a multi-platform ecosystem consisting of an offline-first mobile/tablet field app, a central administration portal, and asynchronous API sync pipelines. This established an end-to-end verifiable framework backed by strict software security and quality checks.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">The Impact</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">Acted as the central engine for engineering and design alignment, delivering 100% adoption across targeted cross-market pilots while establishing:</p>
      <ul class="case-field-list">
        <li>Robust Client-Server Architecture (Offline-to-Cloud API Gateways)</li>
        <li>Strict Pre-Launch Testing Evidence &amp; Cyber-Security Protocols</li>
        <li>Multi-Stakeholder Reporting Matrix (Engineers, Executives, and Global Partners)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section">
    <h2 class="case-section-title">2. Strategy, Agile Cadence &amp; Discovery</h2>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Insight &amp; Requirements Gathering</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">Partnered directly with the Chief Scientific Officer to decompose highly complex environmental and geospatial auditing parameters into concrete, data-dense technical Product Requirement Documents (PRDs). By translating abstract business logic into structural backlog line items, we removed engineering blockages and structured clear use cases for development sprints.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Stakeholders &amp; Team Leadership</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">After establishing the core application architecture, I stepped up to lead the cross-functional delivery roadmap as Senior PM. I managed the design-to-development-to-rollout pipeline in a fast-paced environment, serving as the main liaison between engineering, legal compliance teams, and executive management to coordinate dependencies.</p>
      <ul class="case-field-list" style="margin-top: 16px;">
        <li><strong>Supervisor (CTO):</strong> <a class="case-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/justinbaird/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Justin Baird</a></li>
        <li><strong>Tech Lead:</strong> Ray Chang</li>
        <li><strong>Lead Dev:</strong> Sing, <a class="case-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/phi-le-kim-03697424b/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Phi</a></li>
        <li><strong>Designers:</strong> <a class="case-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/jess-southey/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Jess</a>, <a class="case-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/my-ha-nguyen/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">My Ha</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Constraints &amp; Release Cadence</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">The project operated under intense release schedules requiring reliable software updates shipped to rugged, remote regions. This demanded a zero-tolerance policy for production bugs, forcing our sprint planning to center entirely around deterministic test case pipelines and strict version control.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section">
    <h2 class="case-section-title">3. Technical Execution &amp; Rollouts <span class="case-section-sub">(The &ldquo;How&rdquo;)</span></h2>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label" id="system-map-title">System Mapping</h3>
      <figure class="system-map" aria-labelledby="system-map-title" aria-describedby="system-map-caption">
        <div class="system-map__viewport" role="region" aria-label="System iteration loop">
        <div class="system-map__loop">
          <svg class="system-map__arrows" viewBox="0 0 920 620" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true">
            <defs>
              <marker id="system-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                <path d="M1 1 9 5 1 9" />
              </marker>
            </defs>
            <path d="M260 190 H328" marker-end="url(#system-arrow)" />
            <path d="M590 190 H658" marker-end="url(#system-arrow)" />
            <path d="M790 190 V530 H592" marker-end="url(#system-arrow)" />
            <path d="M330 530 H130 V382" marker-end="url(#system-arrow)" />
          </svg>
        <div class="system-map__inputs">
          <div class="system-map__node">
            <p class="hud-label hud-label--signal">Start // 01</p>
            <h4>Field app</h4>
            <p>Technicians conduct field sampling and examinations.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="system-map__node">
            <p class="hud-label hud-label--signal">02 // Community scouting</p>
            <h4>Mobile observation app</h4>
            <p>Community-led observations and scouting by non-technical staff.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="system-map__node system-map__node--edge">
          <p class="hud-label hud-label--signal">03 // Portable data center</p>
          <h4>Verity Edgecase</h4>
          <p class="system-map__alias">VSC &mdash; Verity Sync Case</p>
          <p>Data backup and offline / online sync. Acts as a portable data center during field trips.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="system-map__node system-map__node--cloud">
          <p class="hud-label hud-label--signal">05 // Central data hub</p>
          <h4>Cloud data center</h4>
          <p>All data syncs back here when devices are online.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="system-map__node system-map__node--admin">
          <p class="hud-label hud-label--signal">04 // Administration</p>
          <h4>Admin dashboard</h4>
          <p>Field-trip setup, data-field management, report generation, and analysis.</p>
        </div>
        <p class="system-map__label system-map__label--backup">Local backup</p>
        <p class="system-map__label system-map__label--sync">Online sync</p>
        <p class="system-map__label system-map__label--review">Review &amp; analysis</p>
        <p class="system-map__label system-map__label--return">Set up the next field trip</p>
        </div>
        </div>
        <figcaption class="case-field-value" id="system-map-caption">A continuous fieldwork loop, not a one-way pipeline: field and community observations are backed up through VSC, data syncs to the cloud when devices are online, and dashboard review and setup inform the next field trip. The loop runs horizontally on desktop and vertically on mobile.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Core Product Decisions</h3>
      <ul class="case-field-list">
        <li><strong>Deconstructed Feature Map:</strong> Broke down unstructured, massive scientific parameters into manageable API contracts and micro-workflows, allowing the platform to support evolving client requirements natively.</li>
        <li><strong>Client-Server Resilience:</strong> Spearheaded the development of an "Offline-First" client-server mobile architecture, ensuring full structural functionality without a network, coupled with automated edge-queue synchronization mechanisms.</li>
        <li><strong>Edge Token Automation:</strong> Engineered a metadata-driven validation engine utilizing automated GPS and camera hardware verification protocols to validate data authenticity before syncing with the central database.</li>
        <li><strong>Rigorous Rollout Governance:</strong> Established the platform's release criteria, enforcing a mandatory protocol where no build progressed to production without clearing exhaustive regression testing, automated code scans, and complete vulnerability patches.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Quality Assurance &amp; Stakeholder Demos</h3>
      <ul class="case-field-list">
        <li><strong>Test &amp; Demo Runways:</strong> Orchestrated comprehensive sprint validation cycles. I personally structured pre-release "runways"—ensuring all technical test cases were systematically completed and verified through explicit testing evidence reports.</li>
        <li><strong>Vulnerability &amp; Security Scans:</strong> Integrated security scanning and loophole detection checks into the release pipeline, verifying code integrity to guarantee zero critical security leaks or data intercept risk prior to live executive stakeholder demos.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Visual Highlights</h3>
      <div class="gallery-wrap" role="region" aria-label="Verity Nature MRV product screens and field-trip photos">
        <div class="gallery-track-wrap">
          <div class="gallery-track" id="galleryTrack">
            {updatedScreenshots.map((src, i) => (
              <img class="gallery-img" src={src} alt={`Verity Nature MRV product screenshot ${i + 1}`} loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            ))}
            <img class="gallery-img" src="/assets/projects/verity-nature-mrv/Select%20download%20package%20screen.png" alt="Verity Nature MRV download package selection screen" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <img class="gallery-img" src="/assets/projects/verity-nature-mrv/Downloading%20package%20screen.png" alt="Verity Nature MRV package download progress screen" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <img class="gallery-img" src="/assets/projects/verity-nature-mrv/VSC%20Release%20October%202023.png" alt="VSC release overview from October 2023" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <img class="gallery-img" src="/assets/projects/verity-nature-mrv/tablet-field-app.jpg" alt="Tablet field app" />
            <img class="gallery-img" src="/assets/projects/verity-nature-mrv/data-syncing-field-trip.jpg" alt="Data syncing during field trip" />
            <img class="gallery-img" src="/assets/projects/verity-nature-mrv/justin-baird-and-the-portable-data-backup.avif" alt="Justin Baird and the portable data backup" />
            <img class="gallery-img" src="/assets/projects/verity-nature-mrv/verity-nature-mrv-field-trip.avif" alt="Verity Nature MRV field trip" />
            <img class="gallery-img" src="/assets/projects/verity-nature-mrv/visit-nursery-darwin.jpg" alt="Visit to nursery in Darwin" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="gallery-controls">
          <button class="gallery-btn" id="galleryPrev" aria-label="Previous">&#8592; Back</button>
          <span class="gallery-counter" id="galleryCounter">1 / {updatedScreenshots.length + 8}</span>
          <button class="gallery-btn" id="galleryNext" aria-label="Next">Next &#8594;</button>
        </div>
      </div>
  
    </div>
  </section>



  <section class="case-section">
    <h2 class="case-section-title">Publications</h2>
    <div class="case-field">
      <ul class="case-field-list">
        <li><a class="case-link" href="https://www.veritynature.com/news/blue-carbon-restoration-project" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Blue Carbon Restoration Project — Verity Nature</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</MissionLayout>

<style>
  .system-map {
    margin: 20px 0 0;
    padding: clamp(16px, 3vw, 32px);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    background: rgba(5, 12, 18, 0.65);
  }
  .system-map__viewport { overflow-x: auto; overscroll-behavior-x: contain; }
  .system-map__loop {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 28.26% 7.61% 28.26% 7.61% 28.26%;
    grid-template-rows: 380px 60px 180px;
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 760px;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
  .system-map__arrows { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.5; pointer-events: none; }
  .system-map__inputs { grid-column: 1; grid-row: 1; display: grid; gap: 16px; z-index: 1; }
  .system-map__node {
    padding: 18px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--bg-panel);
  }
  .system-map__node h4 { margin: 10px 0; font-size: clamp(16px, 2vw, 20px); line-height: 1.4; }
  .system-map__node > p:not(.hud-label) { color: rgba(247, 255, 199, 0.8); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.65; }
  .system-map__node .system-map__alias { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .system-map__node--edge { grid-column: 3; grid-row: 1; align-self: center; z-index: 1; border-color: var(--accent); }
  .system-map__node--cloud { grid-column: 5; grid-row: 1; align-self: center; z-index: 1; border-color: var(--accent-hi); background: #0c251d; }
  .system-map__node--admin { grid-column: 3; grid-row: 3; z-index: 1; }
  .system-map__label {
    position: absolute;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--text-2);
  }
  .system-map__label--backup { left: 28.26%; top: 140px; width: 7.61%; }
  .system-map__label--sync { left: 64.13%; top: 140px; width: 7.61%; }
  .system-map__label--review { left: 67.39%; top: 540px; width: 18.48%; }
  .system-map__label--return { left: 15.22%; top: 540px; width: 19.56%; }
  .system-map figcaption { margin-top: 24px; font-size: 14px; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .system-map__viewport { overflow: visible; }
    .system-map__loop {
      min-width: 0;
      grid-template-columns: 24px minmax(0, 1fr);
      grid-template-rows: repeat(8, auto);
    }
    .system-map__arrows { display: none; }
    .system-map__loop::before {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      left: 0;
      top: 28px;
      bottom: 20px;
      width: 24px;
      border: 1px solid var(--accent);
      border-right: 0;
      border-radius: 12px 0 0 12px;
    }
    .system-map__loop::after {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      left: 15px;
      top: 24px;
      width: 8px;
      height: 8px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--accent);
      border-right: 1px solid var(--accent);
      transform: rotate(45deg);
    }
    .system-map__inputs { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 1; }
    .system-map__node { padding: 14px; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    .system-map__node--edge { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 3; }
    .system-map__node--cloud { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 5; }
    .system-map__node--admin { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 7; }
    .system-map__label { position: static; width: auto; grid-column: 2; padding: 12px 0; }
    .system-map__label::before { content: '\2193'; display: block; color: var(--accent-hi); font-size: 22px; }
    .system-map__label--backup { grid-row: 2; }
    .system-map__label--sync { grid-row: 4; }
    .system-map__label--review { grid-row: 6; }
    .system-map__label--return { grid-row: 8; }
    .system-map__label--return::before { content: '\21B6'; }
  }
</style>
